# Admin icon & badge colors

Lucide icons use `currentColor`. Always set semantic text classes on the icon or its interactive parent.

## Lucide icons

- Default: `text-muted-foreground` on controls (chevrons, menu, theme toggle parent).
- Active/emphasis: `text-foreground` or `text-primary`.
- Do NOT use `text-white`, `text-black`, or fixed `text-zinc-*` / `text-gray-*` unless the icon sits on a guaranteed dark media overlay (e.g. blurred image reveal).

## Dropdown / select icons

- ChevronDown, ChevronUp, Check in shared Select: `text-muted-foreground` or `text-foreground`.
- Never rely on `opacity-50` alone without a semantic text color.

## Status badges & chips

- Use light/dark pairs: `text-{color}-700 dark:text-{color}-400` (and matching borders/backgrounds).
- Or semantic tokens: `text-warning-foreground`, `text-success-foreground`, `text-destructive-foreground`.
- Do not use a single fixed palette step (e.g. only `text-zinc-400`) for both themes.

## CSS variables

- Prefer tokens from `apps/admin/app/globals.css`: `--foreground`, `--muted-foreground`, `--popover-foreground`, `--warning`, `--success`, `--destructive`.
- When adding new popover/dropdown UI, ensure `--popover` and `--popover-foreground` exist before using `text-popover-foreground`.

## Auth login icons

- Password toggle (Eye/EyeOff): use `text-auth-form-input-icon` with hover `text-auth-form-title`; keep `--auth-form-input-icon` readable on light input backgrounds in both `:root` and `.dark`.
